# 37. MITM AND CIA

Remember:

```text
READ   → Confidentiality
CHANGE → Integrity
DROP   → Availability
```

---

# 38. EXAMPLE

A victim sends:

```text
HTTP:
username=alice
password=example
```

If an attacker successfully intercepts plaintext HTTP:

```text
Victim
   ↓
Attacker
   ↓
Server

Attacker may observe:
username=alice
password=example
```

With properly protected HTTPS:

```text
Victim
   ↓
Encrypted TLS
   ↓
Attacker
   ↓
Encrypted traffic
   ↓
Server
```

The attacker may see metadata but should not simply obtain the application plaintext.

