# 59. MITM LIMITATIONS

ARP spoofing does not automatically allow:

- Reading properly encrypted HTTPS content
- Breaking TLS
- Recovering passwords from encrypted traffic
- Bypassing authentication
- Compromising the victim

MITM positioning is only one stage.

---

# 60. IMPORTANT DISTINCTION

```text
MITM POSITION
     ≠
TLS COMPROMISE
```

Being in the network path does not automatically defeat encryption.

---

# 61. COMMON EXAM CONFUSIONS

### ARP

```text
IP → MAC
```

### DNS

```text
Name → IP
```

### ARP Spoofing

```text
Fake IP → Attacker MAC
```

### DNS Spoofing

```text
Fake Name → Wrong IP
```

### MITM

```text
Attacker positioned between communicating parties
```

