# 62. ARP SPOOFING VS DNS SPOOFING

| Feature | ARP Spoofing | DNS Spoofing |
|---|---|---|
| Target | Local IP/MAC mapping | Name/IP resolution |
| Layer/concept | Local network/link operation | Application/network naming service |
| Goal | Redirect local traffic | Redirect domain requests |
| Common use | MITM positioning | Redirection/impersonation |
| Defense | DAI, segmentation, monitoring | DNS security, validation, secure DNS |

---

# 63. MITM VS PHISHING

### MITM

Attacker positions themselves in the communication path.

### Phishing

Attacker tricks the user into interacting with a malicious message/site.

They can sometimes be combined.

Example:

```text
Phishing
   ↓
Victim connects to attacker
   ↓
MITM opportunity
```

---

# 64. MITM VS EVIL TWIN

### Evil Twin

Fake wireless network.

### MITM

Attacker positioned between communication endpoints.

An Evil Twin can be used to facilitate a MITM attack.

